      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To investigate the clinical features and risk factors associated with interstitial lung disease (ILD) in patients with classic dermatomyositis (classic DM) or clinical amyopathic dermatomyositis (CADM)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Medical records of 121 DM patients (77 with classic DM and 44 with CADM) were reviewed retrospectively. The risk factors associated with ILD were identified through Binary Logistic Regression analyses."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "ILD presented in 40. 3% (31/77) of patients with classic DM and 50. 0% (22/44) of patients with CADM. Overall, the DM patients had a prevalence of ILD of 43. 8%. Univariate analyses showed that arthralgia, cough, dyspnea, anti-Jo-1 antibody, malignant tumors, and the levels of Erythrocyte sedimentation rate (ESR) and Albumin (ALB) were associated with ILD. The Multivariate Logistic Regression analysis identified arthralgia (beta= 1. 119, P= 0. 023), cough (beta= 2. 423, P= 0. 003) and ESR (beta= 0. 041, P= 0. 009) as risk factors of ILD."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "ILD is a common complication of classic DM/CADM and arthralgia, cough and high level of ESR are independent risk factors of ILD."
        }
      ]},
